      "source": [
        "Logarithmic transformation is a useful technique for converting a dataset with a highly skewed distribution into a more balanced one.\n",
        "\n",
        "When dealing with variables that exhibit non-linear relationships, the resulting errors may be negatively skewed. Ideally, we aim to minimise these errors when making predictions, while also avoiding overfitting the model.\n",
        "\n",
        "Overfitting occurs when a model becomes too complex by accounting for too many factors, resulting in poor generalisation to new data.\n",
        "\n",
        "By applying a logarithmic transformation to one or more variables, we can improve the accuracy of our model by reshaping the data distribution so that it approximates a normal, bell-shaped curve.\n",
        "\n",
